title: Hide things in the Scene view
intro: Hide a pause menu, a dialogue box or a tilemap layer while you edit, so it stops covering the level. The game still shows it.
project: Platformer | Scene Hide

chapter: The pause menu covers the level | Every click lands on it
look: 0, 0, 5
say: This level's pause menu is laid out right in the middle of it, over the platforms underneath.
say: Say we want to pick the platform under its left side.
sceneclick: -2.5, -1.6
expectselected: Paused
explain: entity:Paused | Picked the menu | The click lands on the menu instead. It covers just what we're trying to work on.

chapter: Hide it | The eye by its row in the Hierarchy
say: Every row in the Hierarchy now has an eye that shows when you hover over it.
click: eye:Paused
explain: eye:Paused | Hidden | Click it, and the menu is hidden in the Scene view, along with everything inside it.
sceneclick: -2.5, -1.6
expectselected: Platform
explain: world:-3, -1.25, 1, -1.75 | Picked the platform | Now clicks and box selections go straight to what's underneath.
say: Hiding is only for editing. It's saved with the scene, so the menu stays out of the way next time, but the game still shows it.
play
wait: 1
tap: Escape
explain: game | Still in the game | Press Escape while playing, and there's the pause menu as usual.
tap: Escape
stop

chapter: H hides the selection | Or Entity, Hide
select: Platform
sceneclick: -2.5, -1.6
key: H
say: Press H in the Scene view, and whatever is selected hides too.
sceneclick: -2.5, -1.6
expectselected: Backdrop
say: Now a click there falls through to the backdrop behind the platform.
select: Platform
menu: Entity > Hide
say: Entity, Hide, shows it again when everything selected is already hidden. Each change is one undo step.
select: Paused
menu: Entity > Hide
explain: scene | Back again | And the pause menu is back, ready to lay out.
